For an arbitrary basis `e : Module.Basis κ ℝ V` (κ finite), the Gram matrix `G i j = form (e i) (e j)`. The raised endomorphism `R = raiseIndex ricci` (defined via the *orthonormal* basis of the metric datum) satisfies `form (R X) Y = Ric Y X` (for symmetric Ric: `= Ric X Y`). Its matrix in the basis `e`: if `R (e j) = ∑ i, A i j • e i`, then `tr R = ∑ i, A i i`. We want `tr R = ∑ i j, G⁻¹ i j Ric (e i) (e j)`. 

