```lean
/-- **Missing dependency 1: evolution of the Levi-Civita connection.**
A connection velocity `connVel t X Y = ∂ₜ (∇_t)_X Y` together with the directional-derivative
calculus `dirh` for the metric-velocity tensor field, satisfying the linearized Koszul formula.
The calculus `dirh` (directional derivatives of the variation tensor) is exactly the first-order
manifold structure that the abstract algebraic setting does not carry. -/
structure LeviCivitaEvolution (h : ℝ → V → V → ℝ) where
  connVel : ℝ → V → V → V
  connVel_add₁ : ∀ t (X X' Y : V), connVel t (X + X') Y = connVel t X Y + connVel t X' Y
  connVel_smul₁ : ∀ t (a : ℝ) (X Y : V), connVel t (a • X) Y = a • connVel t X Y
  connVel_add₂ : ∀ t (X Y Y' : V), connVel t X (Y + Y') = connVel t X Y + connVel t X Y'
  connVel_smul₂ : ∀ t (a : ℝ) (X Y : V), connVel t X (a • Y) = a • connVel t X Y
  hasDeriv : ∀ t X Y, HasDerivAt (fun s => F.nabla s X Y) (connVel t X Y) t
  dirh : ℝ → V → V → V → ℝ
  koszul : ∀ t X Y Z,
    2 * F.metricForm t (connVel t X Y) Z =
      dirh t X Y Z - h t (F.nabla t X Y) Z - h t Y (F.nabla t X Z)
      + dirh t Y X Z - h t (F.nabla t Y X) Z - h t X (F.nabla t Y Z)
      - dirh t Z X Y + h t (F.nabla t Z X) Y + h t X (F.nabla t Z Y)
```

Hmm, the Koszul formula terms: `(∇_X h)(Y,Z) = X(h(Y,Z)) - h(∇_X Y, Z) - h(Y, ∇_X Z)`. In our abstract notation `h t (∇_X Y) Z` is `h_t(∇_X Y, Z)`, and `h t Y (∇_X Z)` is `h_t(Y, ∇_X Z)`. So:
`2 g(A X Y, Z) = dirh X Y Z - h (∇_X Y) Z - h Y (∇_X Z) + dirh Y X Z - h (∇_Y X) Z - h X (∇_Y Z) - dirh Z X Y + h (∇_Z X) Y + h X (∇_Z Y)`.
